# Data Model

## IndexedDB stores

Two object stores, both keyed by `id` (UUID string):

| Store | Key type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `packLists` | `string` | Predefined reusable pack lists |
| `packings` | `string` | Active or completed packing sessions |

## PackList

```ts
type PackList = {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  items: readonly string[];          // ordered list of item text strings
  referencedListIds: readonly string[]; // IDs of other PackLists included by this list
  sortOrder?: number;
  isMajor?: boolean;
  createdAt: string;                 // ISO 8601
  updatedAt: string;                 // bumped on every syncable write (LWW)
  deletedAt?: string;                // soft-delete tombstone; hidden from UI, synced on reconnect
}
```

### Constraints

- No circular references: before saving, validate the full dependency graph.
- A PackList may only be deleted if no other PackList references it.

## Packing

```ts
type PackingItemStatus = 'pending' | 'packed' | 'discarded' | 'not_used';

type PackingItem = {
  listId: string;   // source PackList id, or '__additional__' for ad-hoc items
  text: string;
  status: PackingItemStatus;
};

type PackingStatus = 'active' | 'done';

type Packing = {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  fromDate: string;                  // ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD)
  toDate: string;                    // ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD)
  packListIds: readonly string[];    // selected root pack-lists
  items: readonly PackingItem[];     // expanded and frozen at creation
  status: PackingStatus;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;                 // bumped on every syncable write (LWW)
  deletedAt?: string;                // soft-delete tombstone; hidden from UI, synced on reconnect
}
```

### Item expansion

When a Packing is created, `packListIds` is resolved recursively:
- Only **leaf lists** (lists with no `referencedListIds`) contribute items.
- Items are grouped by their source `listId` for display.
- The expanded item list is frozen into `items` at creation time (snapshot semantics — later edits to a PackList do not affect an existing Packing).

### Status transitions

- `active` → `done` automatically when no items remain `pending`.
- Item status cycles: `pending` → `packed` → `discarded` → `not_used` → `pending`.
- A Packing is discarded by deletion, not by a status field.

## DB layer

All DB access goes through `src/db/`. Never call `idb` directly from a screen or component.
Functions follow verb-first naming: `getPackList`, `savePackList`, `deletePackList`, `getAllPackings`, etc.

Opening the database is centralised in `src/db/db.ts` (`getDb()`). **Current IndexedDB schema version: 2.**

### Schema bumps

Bump the version in `openDB('x2pack', N, …)` and add `if (oldVersion < N) { … }` inside the `upgrade` callback. Existing migrations:

| Version | Change |
|---|---|
| 1 | Create `packLists` and `packings` object stores |
| 2 | Rename legacy packing `date` → `fromDate` / `toDate` |

Rules for new migrations:

- **Cumulative blocks only** — never delete an old `oldVersion < N` block; users may upgrade from any prior version.
- **Stay inside the upgrade transaction** — no `async`/`await` in the migration path; use raw IDB cursors (`unwrap(transaction).objectStore(…)`, `onsuccess`, `cursor.continue()`) so Firefox does not auto-commit early.
- **Test with fake-indexeddb** — seed at `N-1` in `db.test.ts`, call `getDb()`, assert migrated records.
- **Sync impact** — if stored shape or store layout affects P2P, update `protocol.ts`, `syncHandlers.ts`, and `syncArchitecture.ts` in the same change.

There is no migration module per version; keep blocks in `db.ts` unless a bump grows large enough to extract a named helper called synchronously from the upgrade callback.

## P2P sync (local)

Phones on the same network can sync in real time over WebRTC. Full architecture (pairing, wire protocol, LWW, soft deletes, item union merge): **`src/sync/syncArchitecture.ts`**.

- User writes → `emitSync` → DataChannel → peer applies via `*Direct` helpers.
- `getAll*ForSync()` includes soft-deleted tombstones for reconnect; `getAll*()` filters them for UI.
- Sync messages include `protocolVersion`; peers warn or reject on mismatch (see `src/sync/protocol.ts`).
